:::


We can create a logical (see @sec-variable_types) column showing if *H. tumulorum* is detected or undetected at each site using `mutate()` based on the `n_observed` column - if `n_observed` is > 0, this species was detected. 

We also need to join with the site metadata table to get the additional info about the sampling sites. The code below will give us one row for each site including a column, `detected` which is FALSE if *H. tumulorum* is absent and TRUE if it is present.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ht_df <- ht_counts |>
  mutate(detected = n_observed > 0) |>
  left_join(site_metadata)

gt(head(ht_df))
```

